# L §7.1 The literal rule: inline figures include "integer offsets in key arithmetic ... and the same integer
# in the guard that protects the read (`pos(k) > 12`, `pos(k) == 12`, §5.11)".  The read is x[k - 1]; a guard
# `pos(k) > 2` holds a figure that is no offset of the def: LOAD-LITERAL.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

index ks = 1..3
input step: int

def x[k in ks]: int at reader
  rule base = step
  rule a beats base = x[k - 1] + step when pos(k) > 2

ask q: x[3] law 2026-06-30
=== expect
refused: LOAD-LITERAL figure 2 in a rule ...
